📤 Export one complete stored trace as OTLP JSON. Includes resource/scope context and all retained members, regardless of the current search or time window. Writes exact response bytes without a trailing newline; redirect stdout to save a file.

USAGE
  otel-desktop-viewer export trace <id> [flags]

EXAMPLES
  otel-desktop-viewer export trace <id> > trace.json

FLAGS
      --endpoint string   Running viewer HTTP endpoint (default "http://localhost:8000")

GLOBAL FLAGS
  -h, --help   Help for this command
